1
00:05:06,315 --> 00:05:12,315
The Call is a horror, thriller film directed by Timothy Woodward Jr..

2
00:10:12,631 --> 00:10:18,631
In the fall of 1987, a group of small-town friends must survive the night in
the home of a sinister couple after a tragic accident occurs.

3
00:15:18,947 --> 00:15:24,947
Needing only to make a single phone call, the request seems horribly ordinary
until they realize that this call could change their life…or end it.

4
00:20:25,263 --> 00:20:31,263
Edith Cranston, played by Lin Shaye.

5
00:25:31,578 --> 00:25:37,578
Edward Cranston, played by Tobin Bell.

6
00:30:37,894 --> 00:30:43,894
Chris, played by Chester Rushing.

7
00:35:44,210 --> 00:35:50,210
Tonya, played by Erin Sanders.

8
00:40:50,526 --> 00:40:56,526
Harliss, played by Judd Lormand.

9
00:45:56,842 --> 00:46:02,842
Zack, played by Mike C. Manning.

10
00:51:03,157 --> 00:51:09,157
The Call of the Wild is a 2020 American adventure film directed by
Chris Sanders from a screenplay by Michael Green.

11
00:56:09,473 --> 00:56:15,473
It is based on the 1903 novel of the same name by Jack London.

12
01:01:15,789 --> 01:01:21,789
The film stars Harrison Ford, Omar Sy, Cara Gee, Dan
Stevens, Karen Gillan, and Bradley Whitford.

13
01:06:22,105 --> 01:06:28,105
Set during the 1890s Klondike Gold Rush, the film follows a dog named Buck as he is stolen from his home in
California and sent to the Yukon, where he befriends an old outdoorsman and begins a life-altering adventure.

14
01:11:28,421 --> 01:11:34,421
The Call of the Wild was released in the United States on February 21, 2020, by
20th Century Studios (its first film under the company's new name).

15
01:16:34,736 --> 01:16:40,736
It received mixed-to-positive reviews from critics, who praised Ford's performance, John Powell’s music and the
"entertaining action and earnest tone" but criticized the "uncanny valley" effect of the CGI animals.

16
01:21:41,052 --> 01:21:47,052
The film's release was cut short due to the COVID-19 pandemic, grossing $111.1 million against a
production budget of $125–150 million, and lost the studio an estimated $50–100 million.

17
01:26:47,368 --> 01:26:53,368
The film explores themes of missing child, phone call, 1980s.

18
01:31:53,684 --> 01:31:59,684
The tone is dark and intense.
